  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** KULR’s lithium-battery safety solutions are gaining traction in defense, space, AI data centers, and drones, with recent prototype wins and broadening product sales reflecting strong end-market demand. The company’s differentiated thermal-management IP and small-cap profile have fueled takeover speculation, underscoring its perceived strategic value in critical infrastructure.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** CEO Michael Mo’s shareholder letter emphasizes building a battery platform for physical AI, while new CFO and board appointments signal a push for financial discipline and sales execution. The leadership reset follows a period of share-price weakness, and the direct communication aims to restore credibility, though tangible commercial scaling remains the next milestone.",
